# Vulnerability details

## Impact

Losses are double counted and vault participants lose funds

## Proof of Concept

https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-02-ethos/blob/73687f32b934c9d697b97745356cdf8a1f264955/Ethos-Vault/contracts/ReaperVaultV2.sol#L499-L538

        if (_roi < 0) {
            vars.loss = uint256(-_roi);
            _reportLoss(vars.stratAddr, vars.loss); @audit-issue loss removed once
        } else if (_roi > 0) {
            vars.gain = uint256(_roi); 
            vars.fees = _chargeFees(vars.stratAddr, vars.gain);
            strategy.gains += vars.gain;
        }

        ...

        // Profit is locked and gradually released per block
        // NOTE: compute current locked profit and replace with sum of current and new
        vars.lockedProfitBeforeLoss = _calculateLockedProfit() + vars.gain - vars.fees;
        if (vars.lockedProfitBeforeLoss > vars.loss) {
            lockedProfit = vars.lockedProfitBeforeLoss - vars.loss; @audit-issue loss double counted
        } else {
            lockedProfit = 0;
        }

When a loss is reported by the strategy is the loss is first removed from totalAllocated via _reportLoss. Additionally the loss is also removed from the lockedProfits. This is problematic because if there is locked profit then the it will unfairly be double counted and the share accounting will be incorrect. 

## Tools Used

Manual Review

## Recommended Mitigation Steps

_reportLoss should first remove the loss from the locked profit then only remove it from totalAllocated if there isn't enough locked profits to cover the entire loss.

