# Vulnerability details

## Impact
Function `_freeFunds()`  calculates the amount of free funds available after profit locking and it's used to for calculating share price, issuing shares during deposit, or burning shares during withdrawal.

Value returned by `_freeFunds()` is time-dependant, because value returned by `_calculateLockedProfit()` depends on **WHEN** it is called.

    function _freeFunds() internal view returns (uint256) {
        return balance() - _calculateLockedProfit();
    }

Function `_calculateLockedProfit()` calculates the amount of locked profit from recent harvests and it returns a value that depends on time from `lastReport`.

    function _calculateLockedProfit() internal view returns (uint256) {
        uint256 lockedFundsRatio = (block.timestamp - lastReport) * lockedProfitDegradation;
        if (lockedFundsRatio < DEGRADATION_COEFFICIENT) {
            return lockedProfit - ((lockedFundsRatio * lockedProfit) / DEGRADATION_COEFFICIENT);
        }
        return 0;
    }

`lastReport` is updated when a strategy interacts with the vault during its harvest by calling function `report()` profit/loss as well as any repayment of debt.

This is the snippet from `report()` function where `lockedProfit` is updated:

        vars.lockedProfitBeforeLoss = _calculateLockedProfit() + vars.gain - vars.fees;
        if (vars.lockedProfitBeforeLoss > vars.loss) {
            lockedProfit = vars.lockedProfitBeforeLoss - vars.loss;
        } else {
            lockedProfit = 0;
        }
        strategy.lastReport = block.timestamp;
        lastReport = block.timestamp;

