# Vulnerability details

## Impact

When the sendOath() function is used to transfer OATH gains to the StabilityPool, there is currently no mechanism in place to maintain accountability within the contract. Although the function transfers the requested _OathAmount to the _account address if the caller is the StabilityPool contract, there is no record of the transfer being made within the contract. The _OathAmount is not deducted from the contract balance

If the _OathAmount is not accounted for in the contract, it means that the balance of OathToken in the contract will be incorrect. This can potentially cause issues in the functioning of the contract and affect the overall system stability

 it is important to ensure that the _OathAmount is properly accounted for in the contract, such as by deducting it from the contract's balance or tracking the amount separately in a data structure

