# Vulnerability details

## Impact
ActivePoolLUSDDebtUpdated(address _collateral, uint _LUSDDebt) in increaseLUSDDebt(address _collateral, uint _amount) and decreaseLUSDDebt(address _collateral, uint _amount) seems lack a "emit" keyword. This can cause the function reverted and every function call increaseLUSDDebt and decreaseLUSDDebt will revert.

## Proof of Concept
    function increaseLUSDDebt(address _collateral, uint _amount) external override {
        _requireValidCollateralAddress(_collateral);
        _requireCallerIsBOorTroveM();
        LUSDDebt[_collateral] = LUSDDebt[_collateral].add(_amount);
        ActivePoolLUSDDebtUpdated(_collateral, LUSDDebt[_collateral]);
    }

    function decreaseLUSDDebt(address _collateral, uint _amount) external override {
        _requireValidCollateralAddress(_collateral);
        _requireCallerIsBOorTroveMorSP();
        LUSDDebt[_collateral] = LUSDDebt[_collateral].sub(_amount);
        ActivePoolLUSDDebtUpdated(_collateral, LUSDDebt[_collateral]);
    }

increaseLUSDDebt(address _collateral, uint _amount) and decreaseLUSDDebt(address _collateral, uint _amount) in ActivePool.sol will emit ActivePoolLUSDDebtUpdated(address _collateral, uint _LUSDDebt) event at the end. However, "emit" keyword is missed as you can see here. All functions call these two functions can revert due to error.

## Tools Used
Manual Review

## Recommended Mitigation Steps
Add "emit" keyword before the event.

