# Vulnerability details

## Impact

High.

A rogue strategist can undermine the revocation of a strategy by updating the `allocBPS` amount before the next `harvest()` call. The `allocBPS` amount is set to zero when a strategy is revoked by calling `setEmergencyExit()`. However, a strategist with the `STRATEGIST` role can update the `allocBPS` amount of a revoked strategy, effectively reversing the revocation.

During an emergency exit, this vulnerability can be particularly severe and cause loss of funds. Timing is crucial in revoking a strategy, and a rogue strategist can exploit this vulnerability to cause financial harm to users.

## Proof of Concept

The `setEmergencyExit()` function in `ReaperBaseStrategyv4.sol` allows the Guardian to revoke a strategy by calling `IVault(vault).revokeStrategy(address(this))`.

```
  function setEmergencyExit() external {
        _atLeastRole(GUARDIAN);
        emergencyExit = true;
        IVault(vault).revokeStrategy(address(this));
    }
```

The `revokeStrategy()` function in `ReaperVaultv2.sol` sets the allocBPS amount of the strategy to zero when a strategy is revoked. 

```
