## Impact
Since initialize function is not protected by an access control modifier like onlyOwner, then anyone can call it or front run it and modify the contract state.

This could be a serious security issue because the initialize function is usually intended to be called only once during contract deployment and not afterwards. If anyone is able to call this function at any time, they could potentially modify the contract state and cause unexpected behavior or even result in the loss of user funds.

Attacker can set all configuarions via initialize.

