# Vulnerability details

## Impact
In `ActivePool.sol`, in the `setYieldDistributionParams(...)` function, the sum of `_treasurySplit`, `_SPSplit` and `_stakingSplit` can overflow and thus the sum of the three will no longer equal `10_000`. This means that the owner of the active pool can maliciously use this to allocate more assets than intended. What's more, the transaction can overflow by mistake and the yield might be distributed in unexpected ways.

## Proof of Concept
ActivePool.sol: https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-02-ethos/blob/main/Ethos-Core/contracts/ActivePool.sol
Overflow vulnerable line: https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-02-ethos/blob/main/Ethos-Core/contracts/ActivePool.sol#L145
PoolsTest.js: https://github.com/code-423n4/2023-02-ethos/blob/main/Ethos-Core/test/PoolsTest.js

